{"content_hash": "b1eed45c877a2840", "version_id": 480, "article_id": 48, "level_code": "ja_n1", "lang": "ja", "level": 5, "level_label": "N1 上級", "title": "トランプ氏、ロシア産ディーゼル輸入で合意 ゼレンスキー氏は「プーチンへの贈り物」と非難", "title_zh": "特朗普宣布进口俄罗斯柴油，泽连斯基怒斥：这是送给普京的礼物", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "bbc_business", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm1dwgr666wno?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1550531996-ff3dcede9477?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8dHJ1bXAlMjBhbm5vdW5jZXMlMjBkZWFsfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NjU5MjJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by History in HD on Unsplash", "author": "History in HD", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@historyhd?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/donald-trump-beside-man-in-black-suit-cTz5-T7voqQ?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(292, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(330, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "541c58233a3a"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-10", "word_count": 350, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "トランプ米大統領はロシア産ディーゼルを米国に輸入する合意を発表した。これに対しウクライナのゼレンスキー大統領は、戦争を長引かせる「プーチンへの贈り物」だと強く非難し、欧州の同盟国も同調した。", "lead_zh": "美国总统特朗普宣布达成协议，将进口俄罗斯柴油。乌克兰总统泽连斯基强烈谴责此举是延长战争的“送给普京的礼物”，欧洲盟友也迅速表示支持。", "preview": "トランプ米大統領は九日、ロシア産ディーゼルを米国に輸入する合意を発表した。プーチン大統領が直ちに三十万トンを「米国および世界市場」に放出し、十一月に五十万トン、その後さらに百万トンを供給することに同意したという。米財務省は合意の一環として、ロシア産ディーゼル輸出に対する制裁を来年", "preview_zh": "美国总统特朗普9日宣布达成协议，将进口俄罗斯柴油。据称，普京总统同意立即向“美国和全球市场”投放30万吨，11月再供应50万吨，此后还将追加100万吨。作为协议的一部分，美国财政部预计将把针对俄罗斯柴油出口的制裁暂停至明年4月7日，但俄罗斯在美国银行的资产等仍处于冻结状态。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 470, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/48/ja_n1.mp3", "duration": 70.587, "size_bytes": 427248, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 218, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/480.json", "paragraphs": ["トランプ米大統領は九日、ロシア産ディーゼルを米国に輸入する合意を発表した。プーチン大統領が直ちに三十万トンを「米国および世界市場」に放出し、十一月に五十万トン、その後さらに百万トンを供給することに同意したという。米財務省は合意の一環として、ロシア産ディーゼル輸出に対する制裁を来年四月七日まで停止する見通しだが、米銀にある資産などは依然凍結されたままだ。", "ウクライナのゼレンスキー大統領は、この合意を「終わらせるべき戦争への投資」であり、ロシアの戦争遂行を支えるものだと断じた。ロシアはディーゼルを「さらなるテロ」で返してくるだろうと警告し、ザポリージャとキーウへの夜間攻撃を、合意への「感謝の表明」だと指弾した。欧州連合のカラス外務・安全保障政策上級代表も、制裁停止は「モスクワに戦争を続けるための歳入を与える」と批判し、欧州は圧力を緩めないと明言した。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["美国总统特朗普9日宣布达成协议，将进口俄罗斯柴油。据称，普京总统同意立即向“美国和全球市场”投放30万吨，11月再供应50万吨，此后还将追加100万吨。作为协议的一部分，美国财政部预计将把针对俄罗斯柴油出口的制裁暂停至明年4月7日，但俄罗斯在美国银行的资产等仍处于冻结状态。", "乌克兰总统泽连斯基断言，这份协议是“对一场本应结束的战争的投资”，是在支撑俄罗斯的战争机器。他警告说，俄罗斯会用“更多的恐怖”来回报这些柴油，并指责对扎波罗热和基辅的夜间袭击就是俄方对协议的“感谢表示”。欧盟外交与安全政策高级代表卡拉斯也批评说，暂停制裁“给莫斯科提供了继续战争的收入”，并明确表示欧洲不会放松施压。"], "body": "トランプ米大統領は九日、ロシア産ディーゼルを米国に輸入する合意を発表した。プーチン大統領が直ちに三十万トンを「米国および世界市場」に放出し、十一月に五十万トン、その後さらに百万トンを供給することに同意したという。米財務省は合意の一環として、ロシア産ディーゼル輸出に対する制裁を来年四月七日まで停止する見通しだが、米銀にある資産などは依然凍結されたままだ。\n\nウクライナのゼレンスキー大統領は、この合意を「終わらせるべき戦争への投資」であり、ロシアの戦争遂行を支えるものだと断じた。ロシアはディーゼルを「さらなるテロ」で返してくるだろうと警告し、ザポリージャとキーウへの夜間攻撃を、合意への「感謝の表明」だと指弾した。欧州連合のカラス外務・安全保障政策上級代表も、制裁停止は「モスクワに戦争を続けるための歳入を与える」と批判し、欧州は圧力を緩めないと明言した。", "body_zh": "美国总统特朗普9日宣布达成协议，将进口俄罗斯柴油。据称，普京总统同意立即向“美国和全球市场”投放30万吨，11月再供应50万吨，此后还将追加100万吨。作为协议的一部分，美国财政部预计将把针对俄罗斯柴油出口的制裁暂停至明年4月7日，但俄罗斯在美国银行的资产等仍处于冻结状态。\n\n乌克兰总统泽连斯基断言，这份协议是“对一场本应结束的战争的投资”，是在支撑俄罗斯的战争机器。他警告说，俄罗斯会用“更多的恐怖”来回报这些柴油，并指责对扎波罗热和基辅的夜间袭击就是俄方对协议的“感谢表示”。欧盟外交与安全政策高级代表卡拉斯也批评说，暂停制裁“给莫斯科提供了继续战争的收入”，并明确表示欧洲不会放松施压。", "text": "トランプ米大統領は九日、ロシア産ディーゼルを米国に輸入する合意を発表した。プーチン大統領が直ちに三十万トンを「米国および世界市場」に放出し、十一月に五十万トン、その後さらに百万トンを供給することに同意したという。米財務省は合意の一環として、ロシア産ディーゼル輸出に対する制裁を来年四月七日まで停止する見通しだが、米銀にある資産などは依然凍結されたままだ。 ウクライナのゼレンスキー大統領は、この合意を「終わらせるべき戦争への投資」であり、ロシアの戦争遂行を支えるものだと断じた。ロシアはディーゼルを「さらなるテロ」で返してくるだろうと警告し、ザポリージャとキーウへの夜間攻撃を、合意への「感謝の表明」だと指弾した。欧州連合のカラス外務・安全保障政策上級代表も、制裁停止は「モスクワに戦争を続けるための歳入を与える」と批判し、欧州は圧力を緩めないと明言した。", "vocab": [{"word": "合意", "pos": "noun", "zh": "协议，达成一致", "note": "正式用语，常见于外交、商务报道", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "制裁", "pos": "noun", "zh": "制裁", "note": "国际政治高频词，常与「課す」「停止する」搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "非難", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "谴责，指责", "note": "比「批判」语气更强", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "供給", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "供应，供给", "note": "经济新闻常用，反义词是「需要」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "凍結", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "冻结", "note": "用于资产、资金、制裁等", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "歳入", "pos": "noun", "zh": "财政收入，收入", "note": "财政术语，比「収入」更正式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "急騰", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "暴涨，飙升", "note": "价格、股价等急剧上涨", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "模索", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "摸索，探寻", "note": "常与「する」连用，表示寻求方法", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "懸念", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "担忧，顾虑", "note": "正式表达，比「心配」更书面", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "指摘", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "指出，指摘", "note": "用于提出意见、问题点", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "一環", "pos": "noun", "zh": "一环，一部分", "note": "常以「〜の一環として」出现", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "同調", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "赞同，同调", "note": "表示跟随他人意见或行动", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "異例", "pos": "adj/noun", "zh": "异例，罕见", "note": "形容不寻常、打破惯例的事", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "方向転換", "pos": "noun", "zh": "转向，改变方向", "note": "比喻政策、态度的转变", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "圧力", "pos": "noun", "zh": "压力", "note": "外交上常指施加压力", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "可決", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "通过（法案）", "note": "议会表决通过议案时使用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Trump announces deal for Russian diesel as Zelensky calls it a gift to Putin", "summary_original": "Ukraine's president sharply criticised the move, calling it an \"investment in war that must be ended, not prolonged\".", "body_original": "Trump announces deal for Russian diesel as Zelensky calls it a gift to Putin\nBy\nRachel Clun\n,\nbusiness reporter\n,\nReporting from\nNew York,\nand\nAnthony Zurcher\n,\nNorth America correspondent\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nUpdated 6 hours ago\nUkraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky has condemned Donald Trump's announcement of a deal to import Russian diesel into the US.\nZelensky called it a gift to Russian President Vladimir Putin that amounts to \"an investment in a war that must be ended, not prolonged\", a position quickly backed by Ukraine's European allies.\nTrump said Putin had agreed to release 300,000 tonnes of diesel immediately \"to the American and global marketplace\" followed by 500,000 tonnes in November and another million after that.\nIt is understood the US Treasury is suspending sanctions on Russian diesel exports until 7 April as part of the deal, but other assets like those in American banks are still frozen.\nTrump wrote on his Truth Social platform that a further three million tonnes of Russian diesel would be delivered \"within a short period\", dependent on the condition of its refineries, which have been attacked by Ukraine.\nPutin later said Russia, which introduced a ban on diesel exports earlier this year, was willing to supply both the US and global markets with oil and petroleum products,\nbut his statement did not specify amounts.\nZelensky said Russia would repay the diesel with \"further terror\".\n\"We count on America's fair support for our defence of life, for our defence of people in Ukraine – and on the United States having a correspondingly strong conversation with Russia. A strong one, not a weak one,\" he wrote.\nHe later\npointed to deadly overnight strikes on Zaporizhzhia and Kyiv\nas Russia expressing \"its thanks\" for the agreement.\nAnalysts have questioned whether Russia is capable of providing that quantity of diesel and the extent to which doing so will ease prices for American consumers.\nAnalysis: Trump's shock Russia deal highlights mounting pressure to curb fuel prices\nPublished\n22 hours ago\nRussian glide bomb attack on Zaporizhzhia kills at least 15 people\nPublished\n5 minutes ago\nTim Armitage, an investment strategist at Quilter Cheviot, said the numbers mentioned by Trump were \"relatively small\".\nHe said the first tranche equated to approximately 2.25 million barrels, and daily US consumption was around 3.8 million barrels, \"so it won't make a material difference to pump prices in the US\".\n\"Granted, there are then two more releases to come, but it does appear to be a slightly desperate move by President Trump to try to lower inflation ahead of the midterms.\"\nThe BBC has asked the White House what Russia will get from the US in return for the commitment.\nThe agreement with Russia also opens Trump up to criticism from European allies and pro-Ukraine politicians in the US that the American president is now helping to fund Moscow's war machine.\nThe EU's foreign affairs chief Kaja Kallas said suspending sanctions \"provides Moscow with more revenues to wage war\", adding: \"This is not the time to ease pressure on Russia, and Europe won't.\"\nShe said European foreign ministers intended to approve the biggest set of sanctions on Russia since the start of its full-scale invasion on Monday.\nMeanwhile, a UK government spokesperson said its position \"could not be clearer\" and that it would continue working with international partners to support Ukraine and bring about sustained peace.\n\"We will also maintain pressure on Russia through the toughest sanctions regime ever imposed by the UK, increasing the cost of Putin's aggression and supporting efforts to secure a just and lasting peace.\"\nFriday's announcement is the latest effort from Trump to lower fuel prices in the US ahead of the midterm elections, after months spent grappling with the political consequences of the Iran war.\nThat conflict, which began in February, has sent the cost of petrol and in particular diesel skyrocketing, which has soured his standing with the American public who have been stung by the higher pump prices and knock-on effects that led to across-the-board inflation.\nThe average diesel price in the US is currently $6.28 (£4.74) a gallon, according to the AAA, down from the record high of $6.53 recorded at the end of September.\nShortly after Trump's announcement, the US Treasury formally issued a temporary licence allowing Russian diesel into the market.\nPutin said he had spoken to Trump about the global energy situation on Friday, adding: \"The Russian side confirmed its willingness to supply oil and petroleum products to the US market and global markets at large.\"\nAn envoy for Putin, Kirill Dmitriev, welcomed the deal on social media, saying: \"Russia-US co-operation on diesel and energy will benefit the world.\"\nRussia has this year experienced two waves of severe fuel shortages across the country as a result of Ukrainian drone strikes on Russian oil refineries. Its diesel production has fallen by nearly 30%, according to International Energy Agency estimates.\nTrump has expressed his displeasure over those attacks, blaming them for rising fuel prices.\nBut Zelensky defended the strikes on Friday, saying they were in response to \"Russia's years-long campaign of terror against Ukraine's energy sector\".\n\"Ukraine will not set Russian oil refineries on fire if Russia does not destroy our energy infrastructure,\" he said.\nTrump wants to reduce the cost of fuel as the midterms loom - will it work?\nPublished\n1 day ago\nTrump's Truth Social posts often provide incomplete information, and the details of exactly how Russia will supply this fuel to the global market is unclear.\nBut the announced deal represents a remarkable about-face, as the US Congress recently enacted legislation - signed by the president - to authorise new American sanctions and tariffs on nations that import Russian oil and gas.\nWhat impact the deal with Russia will have on fuel prices also remains unclear. The global benchmark for crude oil, Brent, remains above $103 a barrel. Before the war with Iran, Brent crude was trading at about $73 a barrel.\nWith the looming US elections - which will determine whether Republicans maintain control of Congress - Trump has been searching for ways to ease his Republican party's political pain.\nEarlier this week, he said he was \"thinking about\" suspending the federal tax on gasoline and also announced that he would allow so-called red dye diesel to be used on US highways without facing federal tax.\nTrump has also successfully pressured G7 nations into releasing 100 million barrels of oil and diesel from stockpiles to help ease supply concerns and previously supported calls for a ban on diesel exports from the US.\nRelated topics\nFuel\nCost of Living\nDonald Trump\nVladimir Putin", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T20:58:40.709497", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "トランプ", "s": 0.175, "e": 0.613, "sm": 175, "em": 612, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "米", "s": 0.625, "e": 0.825, "sm": 625, "em": 825, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "大統領", "s": 0.838, "e": 1.488, "sm": 837, "em": 1487, "cs": 5, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "は", "s": 1.5, "e": 1.637, "sm": 1500, "em": 1637, "cs": 8, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "九日", "s": 1.65, "e": 2.35, "sm": 1650, "em": 2349, "cs": 9, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "、", "s": 2.35, "e": 2.538, "sm": 2349, "em": 2537, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "ロシア", "s": 2.538, "e": 2.962, "sm": 2537, "em": 2962, "cs": 12, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "産", "s": 2.975, "e": 3.238, "sm": 2975, "em": 3237, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "ディーゼル", "s": 3.25, "e": 3.688, "sm": 3250, "em": 3687, "cs": 16, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "を", "s": 3.7, "e": 3.825, "sm": 3700, "em": 3825, "cs": 21, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "米国", "s": 3.837, "e": 4.312, "sm": 3837, "em": 4312, "cs": 22, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "に", "s": 4.325, "e": 4.475, "sm": 4325, "em": 4475, "cs": 24, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "輸入", "s": 4.487, "e": 4.775, "sm": 4487, "em": 4774, "cs": 25, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "する", "s": 